# Catching an error (ER2): 'body []T_RAP 'handler runs the body (a
# lambda of @) and, when it stops with an error, the handler, given the
# Error; the handler's outcome is []R_ECOVER v (the trap's value, of the
# body's type), []R_ETRY e (the body again) or []H_ALT e (the error goes
# on, as it was). []E_CODE, []E_MESSAGE and []E_LINE read an Error.
== SOURCE
u:r_ead := { path -> '{ @ -> []N_GET path } []T_RAP '{ e -> []R_ECOVER "" } }
t_ally u:r_ead "no/such/file.txt"
'{ @ -> "mine" []S_IGNAL "oops" } []T_RAP '{ e -> []R_ECOVER []E_CODE e }
'{ @ -> "mine" []S_IGNAL "oops" } []T_RAP '{ e -> []R_ECOVER []E_MESSAGE e }
'{ @ -> 1 + 2 } []T_RAP '{ e -> []R_ECOVER 0 }
== TYPE
u:r_ead : Char -> Char
Int
Char
Char
Int
== RESULT
0
mine
oops
3
